    \textbf{Total Score} = Stars + Forks + Base\\
    \vspace{8pt}
  }}
  \vspace{16pt}

  This composite score provides a balanced view of repository momentum beyond raw star counts alone.
}

\posterbox[ambercard, title={Language Breakdown}
]{name=language, column=1, between=row9 and row13}{
  \fontsize{36}{46}\selectfont
  Python and TypeScript command the top 20, driving the AI and web-tooling ecosystems.
  \vspace{16pt}

  \centering
  \renewcommand{\arraystretch}{1.6}
  \begin{tabular}{l l l}
    \rowcolor{accentamber!20!cardbg} \textbf{Language} & \textbf{Count} & \textbf{Share} \\
    Python & 7 & 35\% \\
    TypeScript & 5 & 25\% \\
    Rust & 2 & 10\% \\
    Others & 6 & 30\% \\
  \end{tabular}
  \vspace{16pt}

  \flushleft
  This highlights a heavy reliance on Python for AI/ML workloads.
}

\posterbox[greencard, title={Key Themes in Trending Repos}
]{name=themes, column=1, between=row13 and bottom}{
  \fontsize{36}{46}\selectfont
  The open-source community is racing to build the infrastructure for AI-augmented software development:
  \vspace{16pt}

  \begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Autonomous coding agents}: AI to autonomously write code, handle issues, and execute tasks (\textit{multica}, \textit{open-agents}, \textit{GenericAgent}).
    \item \textbf{Token optimization}: Slashing LLM token consumption by 60--90\% (\textit{caveman}, \textit{rtk}).
    \item \textbf{Memory \& context management}: Compressing session context and querying knowledge graphs (\textit{claude-mem}, \textit{graphify}).
    \item \textbf{Skill distillation}: Packaging expert mental models as reusable AI skills (\textit{andrej-karpathy-skills}, \textit{nuwa-skill}).
  \end{itemize}
}

